From f4cf1ea2859de41ac3155b99ca065111121c2cad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:12:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-kaanapali: Enable FORCE_MEM_CORE_ON for UFS
 AXI PHY clock

Like on SM8650, SM8750 and Eliza, the UFS AXI PHY clock on Kaanapali
needs FORCE_MEM_CORE_ON for the UFS controller in MCQ mode. Without it
the MCQ configuration (queue base addresses and attributes) does not
survive system suspend: with MCQ enabled, every resume from s2idle
starts with the controller fetching from garbage addresses, an SMMU
fault, a fatal bus error and a host reset, and some of those resets
fail and end in a panic.

The UFS PHY ICE core clock already has the bit set; set it for the UFS
PHY AXI clock as well.

Tested on a Lenovo Legion Tab Y700 Gen 5 with MCQ enabled: the MCQ
registers keep their values over s2idle, and 7 suspend cycles resumed
without a UFS error.

Fixes: d1919c375f21 ("clk: qcom: Add support for Global clock controller on Kaanapali")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-kaanapali.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-kaanapali.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-kaanapali.c
index 21335cd56..bd3fbef8a 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-kaanapali.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-kaanapali.c
@@ -3484,6 +3484,7 @@ static void clk_kaanapali_regs_configure(struct device *dev, struct regmap *regm
 
 	/* FORCE_MEM_CORE_ON for ufs phy ice core clocks */
 	qcom_branch_set_force_mem_core(regmap, gcc_ufs_phy_ice_core_clk, true);
+	qcom_branch_set_force_mem_core(regmap, gcc_ufs_phy_axi_clk, true);
 
 	qcom_branch_set_force_mem_core(regmap, gcc_pcie_0_pipe_clk, true);
 	qcom_branch_set_force_periph_on(regmap, gcc_pcie_0_pipe_clk, true);
